Amazingly, you've *already* partially fulfilled my highest-priority request, which is to have all Shiny-app-related static resources be served in a way that takes advantage of browser caching *across* shiny apps (such as by serving them from a consistent URI and doing nothing to thwart browser caching (if appropriate)).  This is probably the most significant performance enhancement I can think of for Shiny apps.  So, that's absolutely wonderful that you've already done that with the core Shiny resources under <app_dir>/shared.  If it were possible to do that for other Shiny-app-related static resources, that would be just awesome.  Some other examples are:

Other core Shiny server stuff:
__assets__/shiny-server.css
__assets__/shiny-server.js
__assets__/sockjs-0.3.4.min.js

For the DT package I believe:
datatables-bootstrap-1.10.7/dataTables.bootstrap.css
datatables-bootstrap-1.10.7/dataTables.extra.css
datatables-binding-0.1.43/datatables.js
datatables-colVis-1.10.7/dataTables.colVis.min.css
nouislider-7.0.10/jquery.nouislider.min.css
nouislider-7.0.10/jquery.nouislider.min.js?_=<some long integer that might thwart caching>
datatables-colVis-1.10.7/dataTables.colVis.min.js?_=<some long integer that might thwart caching>
datatables-1.10.7/jquery.dataTables.min.js?_=<some long integer that might thwart caching>
datatables-bootstrap-1.10.7/dataTables.bootstrap.min.js?_=<some long integer that might thwart caching>

